  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c9f2e8e5b57bd4bd99f33dd56077c2d1, type: 3}
  m_Name: KB_002_PrinterDriverCode39
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: POSTechSupport::POSTechSupport.Data.KnowledgeArticleSO
  articleId: KB-002
  title: Printer reports Code 39 / device cannot start
  category: 2
  content: "Device Manager \u25B8 'This device cannot start (Code 39)' is a DRIVER
    fault, not a hardware one. Reinstall the printer driver, then confirm with a
    test page.\nBefore you do: open Device Manager and read the actual status. If
    the driver reports OK, the jam is somewhere else \u2014 a port conflict looks
    almost identical from the customer's side (see KB-003). Avoid 'Remove & re-add
    printer' as a first move: if the driver wasn't the cause you end up with a removed
    device on top of the original fault, and the ticket closes Degraded."
  relatedErrorCodes:
  - 39
  - Code 39
  guidanceForIssueIds:
  - P2
